        <h3 class="tbb-origin-title">It Started at the Dinner Table</h3>
        <p>Like most great stories, this one began in the most ordinary of places — a family dinner. Two boys, one plate of cheese, and a thousand questions. What is this? Does it talk? Does it have a name? The characters wrote themselves.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tbb-origin-card">
        <div class="tbb-origin-icon">🧀</div>
        <h3 class="tbb-origin-title">A Dad's Perspective</h3>
        <p>Mrunal wanted to write a story that captured the exact feeling of watching a child be brave enough to try something new — that tiny pause before the bite, then the huge grin after. That moment is the whole book.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tbb-origin-card">
        <div class="tbb-origin-icon">📖</div>
        <h3 class="tbb-origin-title">Written with Love</h3>
        <p><em>Tiny Bite Books</em> is a debut picture book by a first-time author with a very simple goal: to make kids giggle, make parents smile, and remind every little one that curious and brave go hand in hand.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

